---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import Toc from '../components/Toc.astro';
import {withBase} from '../lib/paths';

const toc = [
	{id: 'install', label: 'Install / CLI'},
	{id: 'scan', label: 'Scanner errors'},
	{id: 'chaos', label: 'Chaos Monkey'},
	{id: 'reports', label: 'Reports'},
	{id: 'tui', label: 'TUI'},
	{id: 'server', label: 'Paid server'},
];
---

<DocsLayout
	title="Troubleshooting"
	eyebrow="[ DEBUG ]"
	description="Fix the failures people and agents hit most often with Kuyfi."
>
	<Toc items={toc} />

	<Callout type="info" title="Still stuck?">
		<p>
			Open an issue on GitHub with OS, Node version, Contract ID (Testnet), and the exact
			<code>ScanError.code</code> or CLI stderr. Never paste secret keys.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<h2 id="install">Install / CLI</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Symptom</th>
				<th>Fix</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td><code>kuyfi</code> not found after npm install</td>
				<td>
					Confirm Node ≥ 20; reinstall global package; check npm prefix bin is on
					<code>PATH</code>.
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>PowerShell blocks <code>kuyfi.ps1</code></td>
				<td>
					Use <code>kuyfi.cmd</code> / <code>npm.cmd</code>, or set CurrentUser
					<code>RemoteSigned</code>. See <a href={withBase('/installation')}>Installation</a>.
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>invalid</code> Contract ID</td>
				<td>Must match <code>C</code> + 55 <code>A-Z0-9</code> characters — no lowercase.</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Exit <code>0</code> but findings are CRITICAL</td>
				<td>
					<strong>Not a bug.</strong> Exit codes mean tool success/failure, not severity.
					Parse JSON <code>summary</code> / <code>findings</code> in CI. See
					<a href={withBase('/cli')}>CLI</a>.
				</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2 id="scan">Scanner errors</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Code</th>
				<th>Meaning</th>
				<th>What to try</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td><code>CONTRACT_NOT_FOUND</code></td>
				<td>RPC has no WASM for that ID</td>
				<td>Confirm Testnet deploy; wait for indexing; check typos</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>RPC_UNAVAILABLE</code></td>
				<td>Network / endpoint down</td>
				<td>Check connectivity to soroban-testnet.stellar.org; retry</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>XDR_ALIGN_FAILURE</code></td>
				<td>contractspec parse failed</td>
				<td>
					Contract may lack a standard <code>contractspecv0</code> section (non-SDK or exotic
					build)
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>UNKNOWN</code></td>
				<td>Unclassified failure</td>
				<td>Capture full message; open issue</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2 id="chaos">Chaos Monkey</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Symptom</th>
				<th>Explanation</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td>Lots of PRECONDITION / few findings</td>
				<td>
					Normal: ephemeral account is not an authorized signer. Noise is filtered from the
					findings list on purpose.
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Friendbot / funding fails</td>
				<td>
					3 retries then throw. Testnet faucet hiccup — retry later; check RPC health.
					Headless surfaces as <code>Audit failed: Ephemeral keypair funding failed…</code>
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Many TIMEOUTs</td>
				<td>
					Poll window is 20 × 1s after send. Network congestion or slow confirmations —
					rerun; treat as LOW / inconclusive.
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Function skipped</td>
				<td>
					Unresolved UDT or empty param list for that family — see
					<a href={withBase('/vectors')}>Vectors</a>.
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>“Is my contract safe? Zero findings.”</td>
				<td>
					<strong>No.</strong> Absence of findings ≠ absence of vulns. Black-box coverage is
					partial.
				</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2 id="reports">Reports</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<code>Refusing to overwrite existing file: kuyfi-report-…</code> —
			rename or delete the existing report, then re-export (writes use <code>wx</code>).
		</li>
		<li>JSON and PDF disagree? They shouldn’t — same <code>reportId</code>. Re-export from one run.</li>
		<li>Missing explorer URL? Simulation-only classification never broadcasts.</li>
		<li>CI parse errors? Gate on <code>schemaVersion === "1.0.0"</code> — see <a href={withBase('/report-schema')}>schema</a>.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="tui">TUI</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Chaos Monkey blocked with “Run OSINT Scanner first…” — expected. Scan in this session
			before opening Chaos Monkey.
		</li>
		<li>
			System Logs looks “always green” — <code>LogsScreen</code> is static status text, not
			a live RPC diagnostic stream.
		</li>
		<li>
			Terminal too small (&lt; 70 cols or &lt; 20 rows) → <code>TooSmallNotice</code>; resize
			and continue.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="server">Paid scan server</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Status</th>
				<th>Meaning</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td><code>400</code></td>
				<td>
					<code>INVALID_CONTRACT_ID</code> before paywall — fix the ID shape
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>402</code></td>
				<td>Complete x402 payment (Local402 client quote flow)</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>404</code> / <code>422</code> / <code>502</code> / <code>500</code></td>
				<td>
					Scan failed after auth — body <code>&#123; "error": "&lt;ScanErrorCode&gt;" &#125;</code>;
					<strong>not settled</strong> (payer not charged)
				</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>
	<ul>
		<li><code>PAY_TO</code> missing / secret key → use a public <code>G…</code> only; server exits 1 without it.</li>
		<li>Chaos Monkey over HTTP? Intentionally unsupported.</li>
		<li>Full contract → <a href={withBase('/paid-api')}>Paid scan API</a>.</li>
	</ul>
</DocsLayout>
